* charge-pump bench body (issue #30). run.sh prepends design/netlist/cp_bias.spice and
* design/netlist/cp.spice (the committed exports). Not a design.
* VOUT is held by an ideal source, so i(Vo) is the pump's output current (positive = sourced
* into VOUT). UP/DN are ideal logic with 100 ps edges, amplitude = the corner's own Vdd.
*   40-60 ns   UP only            -> I_up   (avg 50-60 ns)
*   80-100 ns  DN only            -> I_dn   (avg 90-100 ns, negative)
*   105-115 ns idle               -> leakage, and I(Vdd) = bias + idle current
*   120-140 ns UP and DN together -> net current (mismatch)
*   160 ns     one 200 ps UP pulse -> charge per pulse (integral 159-164 ns)
*   180 ns     one 200 ps DN pulse -> charge per pulse (integral 179-184 ns)
*   VOUT 0.6 V until 200 ns, 0.3 V 202-240 ns, 0.9 V 242-280 ns; idle -> dump-buffer VDUMP tracking
Vdd vdd 0 1.2
Vo vout 0 PWL(0 0.6 200n 0.6 202n 0.3 240n 0.3 242n 0.9 300n 0.9)
Bup up 0 V = v(vdd)*pwl(time, 0,0, 40n,0, 40.1n,1, 60n,1, 60.1n,0, 120n,0, 120.1n,1, 140n,1, 140.1n,0, 160n,0, 160.1n,1, 160.3n,1, 160.4n,0)
Bdn dn 0 V = v(vdd)*pwl(time, 0,0, 80n,0, 80.1n,1, 100n,1, 100.1n,0, 120n,0, 120.1n,1, 140n,1, 140.1n,0, 180n,0, 180.1n,1, 180.3n,1, 180.4n,0)
XB ibp icp ibn icn vdd 0 cp_bias
XDUT up dn ibp icp ibn icn vout vdd 0 cp
